# What must never leave this machine.
#
# `vercel --prod` uploads the working DIRECTORY, not a git commit. This project
# has no git remote, so everything here is deployed from local disk — including
# files git has been ignoring all along. `.gitignore` is not reliably consulted
# by the Vercel CLI, so the exclusions are restated here explicitly rather than
# inherited by assumption.
#
# Do not "tidy" this by deleting entries that look redundant with .gitignore.
# The redundancy is the point: one file governs what is committed, the other
# governs what is uploaded, and they are different questions.

# Real financial data. 12,227 cheques, ~PHP 2.9 billion, every vendor the group
# pays, named. The application reads these through an upload form at runtime;
# it never needs them on the server, and they must not sit in a deployment.
*.xlsx
~$*.xlsx

# Credentials. The database URLs, the Acumatica password, and AUTH_SECRET.
# Production values are set in the Vercel dashboard as environment variables —
# a .env file in a deployment would both leak these and silently override them.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local scratch that has no business on a server.
probe-*.mjs
*.log

# Build and test artefacts — Vercel builds from source.
.next
node_modules
coverage
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# The working ledger and plans. Not secret, but not something to serve.
.superpowers
